{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"RESOLVED via Gerrit — landing summary (Phase 2 complete)\n\nRoot cause (proven at runtime): `_cmd_list` and `_cmd_session_logs` in\n`src/rebar/_engine_support/reads_cli.py` gated init on a bare `os.path.isdir(tracker)` and\ncalled `list_states` / `recent_session_logs_state` (`reduce_all_tickets`) directly, bypassing the\nhardened read chokepoint `_reads._tracker`. rapt-dreadable-dromedary (aefe-614a-2631-4117)\nswitched that chokepoint + the write gate to the content-aware `store_is_usable`, but these two\nCLI arms were never updated. A present-but-unusable tracker (marker-files-only: isdir true, no\n`.git`-with-HEAD, no store structure; or mid-clone with unresolvable HEAD) passed bare `isdir`, so\nthe CLI printed `[]` at exit 0 instead of rejecting it — the exact fallback-masking rapt-d removed\nfrom the library, surviving on the CLI surface.\n\nFix: replaced both bare `os.path.isdir(tracker)` gates with\n`rebar._store.store_usability.store_is_usable(tracker)` (reused the authority predicate, invented\nnothing). Zero contract change: ABSENT still rc 1; valid EMPTY still `[]` rc 0; `.git`-less\nSTRUCTURED snapshot still reads; only the unusable shapes flip `[]` rc 0 → rc 1 \"not initialized\".\n\nRED→GREEN: new `tests/unit/test_reads_cli_uninitialized_store.py` drives both CLI arms against a\nmarker-files-only tracker and a mid-clone tracker (assert rc 1 \"not initialized\"), plus\nno-regression (absent rc 1; valid-empty `[]` rc 0) and a structural class guard against\nreintroducing bare `isdir`. Proved RED first (broken/mid-clone wrongly rc 0 `[]`), GREEN after.\nDefect-seeded mutation check inside sandbox-exec killed the reverted gate. End-to-end replicated\nvia the real `rebar list` / `rebar session-logs` binary on a broken store (now rc 1).\n\nAttribution: caused_by = aefe-614a-2631-4117 (obligation creator), close-class regression. Date\ntest: the isdir lines predate rapt-d (2026-06-24 vs 2026-08-29) → unmet-obligation /\nmissed-consumer-update, attributed to the obligation creator, NOT the isdir author.\n\nParity census (Step 7): FIX ×2 (_cmd_list:340, _cmd_session_logs:384). N/A: descendants.py:25\n(deliberately tolerant read), next_batch.py:154 (not a readiness gate; already fails closed rc 1),\nsrc/rebar/_snapshot/repo_snapshot.py:619 (own stronger rev-parse --git-dir probe),\n_engine_support/reads.py:251 (best-effort sync guard). OK: MCP/library channel (funnels through\n_reads._tracker → store_is_usable). Separate finding: CLI search/ready have NO gate at all →\nfiled 97e9-e663-a94e-4038 (discovered_from).\n\nLanded: Gerrit change 2412 (https://rebar.solutions.navateam.com/c/rebar/+/2412),\nmerged as origin/main 91cf9b46ec74. Votes: LLM-Review +1 (PASS, 1 non-blocking advisory),\nVerified +1 (CI success), 0 unresolved. Plan-review: certified (PASS, 0 blocking, 0 advisory).\neb64 conflict check: DISJOINT (fix touches _engine_support/reads_cli.py + new tests/unit test,\nnot in eb64's file_impact) — no collision."},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1788068084786755748,"uuid":"bfa41392-6ad2-4b2d-b08c-b3a111dee305"}